5-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1141361#post1141361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about now?<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022Rage of the Killer Moon </b>: Spend two Essence points (R) per turn, add Purity to attack rolls that ignore defense and dodge rolls, if a superatural power is increasing the enemy defese the rahu ignores one point per purity renown, he still adds his purity on the attack roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless I'm mistaken, werewolves cannot do aggravated damage anymore. If this is a 5th dot in a Moon Gift, then allowing it to perform aggravated would be immensely thematic for something called the &quot;Killer Moon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T03:23:52-07:00","id":1141699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1141530#post1141530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unless I'm mistaken, werewolves cannot do aggravated damage anymore. If this is a 5th dot in a Moon Gift, then allowing it to perform aggravated would be immensely thematic for something called the &quot;Killer Moon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that doing dirrect aggravated damage is theme of the bane element of the game, and bane conditions are more thematic with the tribal lement of the game rather than the auspice. With this whole favored prey part of the Tribes. The fifth dot of the killer moon should escalate like:\u2022attune to the prey, \u2022\u2022 become unstoppable on the hunt and let no wound hinder you, \u2022\u2022\u2022 let the prey know that you come for her and her friends can do nothing to prevent you from doing so, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 grab the prey in a deadly grip with no escape, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 horrible death at the claws and fangs of the killer.<br /> <br /> Actually werewolves can do aggravated damage with a bite attack that devours flesh aka essence with a breaking point towards spirit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T03:50:42-07:00","id":1141703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is that doing dirrect aggravated damage is theme of the bane element of the game </div> </div> </div>Work with that, make it so the 5th level lets you became, temporarily, the Bane of one selected enemy. Add some prerequisites, like having tasted its blood and that you cannot use the power again on a new target until the previous is killed.<br /> <br /> If you make it to last just a Scene, it is a gamble. You have one scene in wich you can mess it up real good, but if it somehow survives, you cannot use the trick again untill you bring it down by other means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T07:08:17-07:00","id":1141734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1141699#post1141699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that doing dirrect aggravated damage is theme of the bane element of the game, and bane conditions are more thematic with the tribal lement of the game rather than the auspice. With this whole favored prey part of the Tribes. The fifth dot of the killer moon should escalate like:\u2022attune to the prey, \u2022\u2022 become unstoppable on the hunt and let no wound hinder you, \u2022\u2022\u2022 let the prey know that you come for her and her friends can do nothing to prevent you from doing so, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 grab the prey in a deadly grip with no escape, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 horrible death at the claws and fangs of the killer.<br /> <br /> Actually werewolves can do aggravated damage with a bite attack that devours flesh aka essence with a breaking point towards spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Urfarah's Bane too. A Killer Moon should have an easier time just... Killing shit. Even if it's your packmates as you go into Kuruth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:38:32-07:00","id":1141763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1141699#post1141699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually werewolves can do aggravated damage with a bite attack that devours flesh aka essence with a breaking point towards spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, sure, but it's not a direct attack like how Vampires have their fun little toys. It's a straight up Harmony-check every time you pull out the bite.<br /> <br /> If you don't want the 5-dot gift to do Agg, that's fine, but it's got to be on that same level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T09:45:05-07:00","id":1141787,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar606_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"606\" data-vbnamecard=\"606\">Aynie</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> = Go go Uratha Aggravated Rangers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you where my players you might have succeeded to convince go towards that direction <br /> The problem is that if I do that with the killer moon then I might have problem with the kinslayer gift list, if a rahu can allready do aggravated damage and be the bane of its kin and far far away even after condiions then there is no reason for a kinslayer gift list. Aggravated damage is about that huge in werewolf.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> good ideas there they do add up to my agenda.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Urfarah's Bane to </div> </div> </div>May it be better for kinslayer gift? Focusing down aggravated damage to the favored prey of tribe rather than an entire auspice?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar606_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"606\" data-vbnamecard=\"606\">Aynie</a><br /> Point taken, though I don't care to compare werewolf gifts with disciplines, they are really not the same at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T23:40:02-07:00","id":1142051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1141787#post1141787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that if I do that with the killer moon then I might have problem with the kinslayer gift list, if a rahu can allready do aggravated damage and be the bane of its kin and far far away even after condiions then there is no reason for a kinslayer gift list. Aggravated damage is about that huge in werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://media3.giphy.com/media/3o85xIO33l7RlmLR4I/200.webp#0-grid1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Kinslayer is different Gift list, will work on slightly different powers and mechanics and even those rare Blood Talons Rahu will have many various Gifts to choose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-20-2017, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T00:50:35-07:00","id":1142062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1141787#post1141787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that if I do that with the killer moon then I might have problem with the kinslayer gift list, if a rahu can allready do aggravated damage and be the bane of its kin and far far away even after condiions then there is no reason for a kinslayer gift list. Aggravated damage is about that huge in werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>You definitively don't want to make Aggravated damage available to a Shadow Gift list to anyone with 1 point in the relevant renown. The prerequisite to it being the pinnacle of Purity is reward enough to Uratha that never actually engaged in the base activity of cannibalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:50:11-07:00","id":1142121,"title":"","content":"Ok I thougt of a different approach.<br /> <b>Fatal Strike</b>: Spend 2 Essence and roll Wits + Survival + Purity as a reflexive action. If the successes of the gift activation equal the remaining health levels of the Target, the attack the rahu does against him counts as a<b> killing blow</b> if it makes contact.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Alternative system</b></u><br /> Spend 2 Essence and roll Wits + Survival + Purity vs Stamina + Trait , if the Rahu wins the next attack on the target if it hits will count as a <b>killing blow</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptonal Success: </b>The werewolf gains back the essence that used to activate the gift and gain the pure condition without the need to flair purity renown with essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The attack fails and the next turn the prey acts as if it succeeded on a <b>Surprise roll</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 09-20-2017, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:02:55-07:00","id":1142125,"title":"","content":"Nope, that's broken, and there's already design space dedicated to it with Efficient Killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:28:56-07:00","id":1142137,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it's broken, just redundant. You're basically just rolling damage, and it counting as a killing blow is unnecessary, since a killing blow does the entire dicepool worth of damage.<br /> <br /> Some magical, better version of Efficient Killer is a good way to go from a design perspective though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:34:12-07:00","id":1142140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1142125#post1142125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, that's broken, and there's already design space dedicated to it with Efficient Killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Efficient killer, is actually, <b>If</b>-ficient killer.<br /> It has too many parameters and can be used by all werewolves who have the prerequisites.<br /> Fatal Strike works on all targets and not only in Gauru. it also has essence expediture and consequences if it drama-fails.<br /> Plus because there is a merit out there with similar effects it doesn't mean that there shouldn't be a gift that does it better out there.<br /> Its like saying that the Crimson spasm shouldn't exist, because allready exists the merits fortifying form, favored form and living weapon.<br /> I think its an awesome 5 dot gift, way weaker than direct aggravated damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:39:27-07:00","id":1142146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1142137#post1142137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're basically just rolling damage, and it counting as a killing blow is unnecessary</div> </div> </div> </div>Its just that there is a chance that the attack roll may fail. Probably the ideal would have been to remove completely the attack roll and just depend on the gift activation<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:29:10-07:00","id":1142164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1142140#post1142140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Efficient killer, is actually, <b>If</b>-ficient killer.<br /> It has too many parameters and can be used by all werewolves who have the prerequisites.<br /> Fatal Strike works on all targets and not only in Gauru. it also has essence expediture and consequences if it drama-fails.<br /> Plus because there is a merit out there with similar effects it doesn't mean that there shouldn't be a gift that does it better out there.<br /> Its like saying that the Crimson spasm shouldn't exist, because allready exists the merits fortifying form, favored form and living weapon.<br /> I think its an awesome 5 dot gift, way weaker than direct aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why it's broken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:12:58-07:00","id":1144392,"title":"","content":"Ok Different Approach.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<b> Primal Killer</b>: Make an attack as normal, if you wound your target with lethal damage, spend 2 essence and roll Strength + Brawl + Purity vs Stamina + Supernatural Trait. The gift may be used only on single targets.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The werewolf kills the victim as if he won in a Down and Dirty Combat.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b> The werewolf also gains back the Essence he spent to activate the gift.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The werewolf enters Basu-im and loses his defense for the next round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 09-27-2017, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T08:29:12-07:00","id":1144426,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T08:45:34-07:00","id":1144438,"title":"","content":"Excellent lets go for the next List, the Shadow Gift of Kinslayer will be far easier to work on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:26:10-07:00","id":1144455,"title":"","content":"Probably wasn't clear there. *shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:31:13-07:00","id":1144461,"title":"","content":"It still has fail chance or worse. Its balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T16:23:36-07:00","id":1144555,"title":"","content":"It's far from balanced. Anything that becomes an instant win button without extremely heavy drawbacks is, frankly, terrible design. There's a reason Efficient Killer isn't popular despite it's many limitations, and that one doesn't even guarantee a kill unlike your suggestion. You should really reconsider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T22:17:06-07:00","id":1144633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1144555#post1144555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason Efficient Killer isn't popular despite it's many limitations</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to be pretty popular, the prerequisites are the difficult part, as they mentioned. I've only seen one person denounce it and plenty others take it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a><br /> <br /> I don't understand your arguments against aggravated damage when this is an instant-kill attack. 5 dots of renown aren't exactly going to be common, and you can balance it out by having it cost 5 Essence for the scene, or one per turn like Crimson Spasm. Call it 'Bane of All Things,' with Luna as Queen of the Shadow granting werewolves the hidden weakness in all things, even those which don't ordinarily have banes. Limit it to claws,if you want, so they won't 'regen' the Essence back via eating, and you have a fairly powerful but not unreasonably so gift that relies entirely on the werewolf's ability to use it while still leaving powerful enemies the opportunity to leave or throw minions in the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T03:43:01-07:00","id":1144690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1144633#post1144633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems to be pretty popular, the prerequisites are the difficult part, as they mentioned. I've only seen one person denounce it and plenty others take it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a><br /> <br /> I don't understand your arguments against aggravated damage when this is an instant-kill attack. 5 dots of renown aren't exactly going to be common, and you can balance it out by having it cost 5 Essence for the scene, or one per turn like Crimson Spasm. Call it 'Bane of All Things,' with Luna as Queen of the Shadow granting werewolves the hidden weakness in all things, even those which don't ordinarily have banes. Limit it to claws,if you want, so they won't 'regen' the Essence back via eating, and you have a fairly powerful but not unreasonably so gift that relies entirely on the werewolf's ability to use it while still leaving powerful enemies the opportunity to leave or throw minions in the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes yes yes I know its broken, its just that I prefere to make the gift to have a relationship with the new rules, rather than just aggravated.<br /> My core idea is to unite the old rank 5 gifts and make a new gift that is none of them.<br /> <br /> What elements the gift must have: <br /> a) it must be used in all forms<br /> b) it must aid the werewolf to kill prey more easily<br /> c)It must be costly, be it like 1st edition luna's fury or 2nd edition crimson spasm, or a 2-3 essence cost but with deadly effect<br /> d)it must have an effect no otger gift has.<br /> <br /> Since you ask for somthing more balanced, Here is something more balanced:<br /> <br /> <b>Pulse of the Killer</b>: The werewolf Spends an Essence point for each character he intents to kill, for the scene the characters that have been marked by the Rahu lose one health level from their health pool for every point of Purity Renown the Werewolf has, they don't take damage, it is just that the Rahu needs to make that less damage in order to kill them, the Rahu may use the gift to as many enemies as his <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Purity Renown dots.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T09:22:01-07:00","id":1144806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1144690#post1144690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes yes yes I know its broken, its just that I prefere to make the gift to have a relationship with the new rules, rather than just aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a relationship with the new rules, though. It's the apex of the 'Killing Moon,' I don't know why you balk at aggravated.<br /> <br /> Either way I left my suggestion there you don't have to go with it.<br /> <br /> But if you're converting these over for a player, you're really giving them powerful and game changing weapons in this conversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T09:53:38-07:00","id":1144817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1144806#post1144806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has a relationship with the new rules, though. It's the apex of the 'Killing Moon,' I don't know why you balk at aggravated.<br /> <br /> Either way I left my suggestion there you don't have to go with it.<br /> <br /> But if you're converting these over for a player, you're really giving them powerful and game changing weapons in this conversion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because if I give to that character direct aggravated damage he will be too much with his allready gigantic damage potential <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I believe the last gift I posted is closer to 2nd edition forsaken, it may still need work but I think is the best so far.<br /> <br /> What do you think ?<br /> Please keep suggesting, you are helpful, you make me think options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:03:18-07:00","id":1144933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1144817#post1144817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because if I give to that character direct aggravated damage he will be too much with his allready gigantic damage potential <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to let you kill anything with just 1 success, despite stuff like say, gargantuan size.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T11:56:02-07:00","id":1145319,"title":"","content":"Not one success, a contested roll <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, unlikely to kill something with gargantuan size, except if you roll insanely well on the activation roll and mange to do damage as well.<br /> <br /> Also I think you haven't noticed this yet: <br /> <br /> <i><b>''Pulse of the Killer</b>: The werewolf Spends an Essence point for each character he intents to kill, for the scene the characters that have been marked by the Rahu lose one health level from their health pool for every point of Purity Renown the Werewolf has, they don't take damage, it is just that the Rahu needs to make that less damage in order to kill them, the Rahu may use the gift to as many enemies as his <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Purity Renown dots.''</span></span></span></i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T15:29:55-07:00","id":1145370,"title":"","content":"Huh, that's a pretty interesting one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T02:20:25-07:00","id":1145472,"title":"","content":"Ok so far,lets say that we have a complete Moon Gift called ''The Killer's Moon Gift''.<br /> What questions you may have so far before working on the ''Gift of the Kinslayer''? (name may change)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T11:38:28-07:00","id":1145590,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about a few things for it. I got stuck with a couple of the renown. One of them, I figured, would allow access to silver claws or fangs, which would be thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> But basing it off the original wolf slayer gift, I figured you could have Cunning penalize extrasensory chances to notice the Gifted werewolf by their Cunning, tied with an ability to spend an Essence to cut the blood tracer ties one gets by tasting a target's blood. Honor would force Uratha you're fighting with from going gauru and into death rage, effectively eliminating triggers on both of you, for Honor dots in turns after your last attack, the effect breaking if you went gauru yourself. Part of me wants to have the ability break if someone else goes gauru nearby, so you could avoid 'one person locks the werewolf down while your six packmates go gauru on him.' I like the idea of one of them, probably Glory, turning your normal regeneration from Bashing to Lethal for a scene at a fairly low cost.<br /> <br /> Really though it's an incredibly niche Gift, hard to find even among spirits. And I wish that the forum's 'lets make new gifts' opportunity would be for unique but prevalent things like Gifts of Fire or Gifts of Murder or Gifts of Greed and the other eight sins and so on. Like even 'Wolf Slaying' seems like it would be better replaced by a Gift of Silver. I appreciate this is driven by your desire to convert a character's gifts, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2017, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T12:45:09-07:00","id":1145607,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> thank you thank you and thank you very much.<br /> And very good starting ideas, you realy gave me something to boost my thinking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T14:02:15-07:00","id":1145626,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>:<br /> <br /> Silver Jaws sounds like Purity. Your Cunning alternative seems to thread over Feet of Mist territory (might need to develop the idea further) - alternatively, use essence to change your blood taste into someone else you've bitten, have those preying on you chase a wild goose. Honor sounds something like &quot;Locked Rage&quot;. Glory could instead make the Lethal regeneration more costly, say, half your glory rounded up in essence before your regeneration can heal lethal damage, likely off a toxin or ichor when damaged. Wisdom could be something to detect Uratha more easily, without having to get that close to catch their spiritual scent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T12:02:28-07:00","id":1145862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1145626#post1145626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Jaws sounds like Purity. Your Cunning alternative seems to thread over Feet of Mist territory (might need to develop the idea further) - alternatively, use essence to change your blood taste into someone else you've bitten, have those preying on you chase a wild goose. Honor sounds something like &quot;Locked Rage&quot;. Glory could instead make the Lethal regeneration more costly, say, half your glory rounded up in essence before your regeneration can heal lethal damage, likely off a toxin or ichor when damaged. Wisdom could be something to detect Uratha more easily, without having to get that close to catch their spiritual scent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are good.<br /> <br /> But I was thinking about it. Wolf Slaying seems like the kind of thing that wouldn't have a spirit. Yet so inherent among werewolves that it would be fitting for a Wolf Gift, instead of a Shadow one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T03:03:39-07:00","id":1146010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1145862#post1145862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are good.<br /> <br /> Wolf Gift, instead of a Shadow one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok now you pumped me up, how about Tribe specific Wolf Gifts ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T05:18:25-07:00","id":1146031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146010#post1146010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok now you pumped me up, how about Tribe specific Wolf Gifts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T08:13:52-07:00","id":1146063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146010#post1146010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok now you pumped me up, how about Tribe specific Wolf Gifts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf Gifts are accessible to every werewolf, but there can be big obstacles to hurdle to get them.<br /> <br /> 'This doesn\u2019t mean that every new Wolf Gift you add to the game has to be widely available, though. As inherent aspects of the werewolf, there\u2019s viable design space around requiring a character to find a way of delving deeper into her spiritual power to access it. A Gift of Essence might require the Uratha to undergo strange, alchemical treatments first, perhaps involving buying a representative Merit. Delving into the blasphemous Gift of Man, that gives dominance over other werewolves just as the human tames and leashes the whipped dog, could be the preserve of those Uratha willing to undergo horrific, self-abasing rituals or to sign on with the Maeljin.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T09:15:45-07:00","id":1146071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146063#post1146063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wolf Gifts are accessible to every werewolf, but there can be big obstacles to hurdle to get them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet there always can be exceptions to the rule, if not, then so be it Tribal shadow gifts direcly from firstborn's brood, or avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T09:32:06-07:00","id":1146075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146071#post1146071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet there always can be exceptions to the rule, if not, then so be it Tribal shadow gifts direcly from firstborn's brood, or avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf gifts aren't tribal specific. Shadow Gift get a price break depending on splat because of certain broods that are prone to unlocking it to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T10:03:44-07:00","id":1146083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146075#post1146075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wolf gifts aren't tribal specific. Shadow Gift get a price break depending on splat because of certain broods that are prone to unlocking it to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I am doing with the kigslayer gift is not in the corebook so please don't bother with canon core book stuff. It is a tribal specfic gift that only blood talons can take and is related to their sacred prey. It can be a wolf gift, or a shadow gift, in any case it will only be for Blood Talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:11:29-07:00","id":1146103,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a> I'll use this collaboration however I please, the same logically applies to you, but if you're going to disregard the design canons entirely guess that's as much use I can get from your input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:38:04-07:00","id":1146109,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're free to make the gift tribal only but if you're posting it here I wouldn't expect that to be followed. We seem to be loosely brainstorming things so might as well go with the flow, obviously nothing keeps you from running it the way you want or others from running it the way they want.<br /> <br /> That said, there's a lot of reasons gifts are open now. A big thing is while the Blood Talons have werewolves as their sacred prey, they are not the only ones who hunt werewolves in sacred hunts. Bone Shadows are likely to target low-Harmony werewolves, for instance. And if you look at the Pure's sacred prey, the Forsaken fit throughout them, so why wouldn't they have it? And obviously, Blood Talons don't only hunt werewolves, and are just as likely to hunt the sacred prey of other tribes. Then you have the lodges, especially pillars, of ghost wolves and other tribes that are likely to bring down werewolves.<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that you get these gifts from spirits. Even if you were to privately cultivate a spirit of a unique idea somehow, it would be impossible to truly keep it isolated from other werewolves.<br /> <br /> That said, there's nothing wrong with giving it prerequisites that a Blood Talon is more likely to have, as the wolf gift noted. An obvious 'having killed a werewolf in fair combat and devoured it whole' would limit access to a wolf gift so that it wouldn't be commonplace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T12:12:48-07:00","id":1146121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146109#post1146109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you're free to make the gift tribal only but if you're posting it here I wouldn't expect that to be followed.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Why not? Afterall this is what this topic is about. Afterall it is about the conversion of a first edition of a tribal gift to the second edition. This is the core theme of the topic. It has a descent follow so far.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146109#post1146109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, there's a lot of reasons gifts are open now. A big thing is while the Blood Talons have werewolves as their sacred prey, they are not the only ones who hunt werewolves in sacred hunts. Bone Shadows are likely to target low-Harmony werewolves, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, werewolves are not hunting only one prey,or only their sacred prey, its just that so far there is not a tribal gift list that boosts their tribal sacred hunting, appart from that, a sacred prey gift list its just another mood element, that you may or may not include in a setting, like anything else in the game. If the rituals are enough for you for example, fine by me, afterall there is a level 5 ritual that allows you to do aggravated to werewolves, you can easily make variations of it for each tribe and allow them to make aggravated to their favored prey. <br /> Also gifts are not that open, not more than the old edition, you are not likely to see a hunter in darkness with weather gifts or a blood talon with elemental gifts. Not that it can't happen but it needs far great effort in roleplaying and experience, like in the old edition, if you find a spirit and you are able to convince it you can gain any gift, given that it is not a Moon gift.<br /> <br /> And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a>, you didn't really understood my last post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T12:49:29-07:00","id":1146132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146121#post1146121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Afterall this is what this topic is about. Afterall it is about the conversion of a first edition of a tribal gift to the second edition. This is the core theme of the topic. It has a descent follow so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because your setting is your setting. You have different needs than other people do when making or running their own games. Gifts are something people can get behind easier, but restrictive rules on said gifts that don't necessarily fit within the setting as written aren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look, werewolves are not hunting only one prey,or only their sacred prey, its just that so far there is not a tribal gift list that boosts their tribal sacred hunting, appart from that, a sacred prey gift list its just another mood element, that you may or may not include in a setting, like anything else in the game. If the rituals are enough for you for example, fine by me, afterall there is a level 5 ritual that allows you to do aggravated to werewolves, you can easily make variations of it for each tribe and allow them to make aggravated to their favored prey. </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't really need to, humans take aggravated from eating, spirits and claimed you find their own bane, and so forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also gifts are not that open, not more than the old edition, you are not likely to see a hunter in darkness with weather gifts or a blood talon with elemental gifts. Not that it can't happen but it needs far great effort in roleplaying and experience, like in the old edition, if you find a spirit and you are able to convince it you can gain any gift, given that it is not a Moon gift. </div> </div> </div>As first edition went on they stopped mentioning whether Gifts were Affinity and Non-Affinity and just said things like they were the 'mainstay' of a lodge or 'Red Wolf's' Gifts. It is basically the same, any werewolf can get any Gift, so why would you make a Gift tribe only?<br /> <br /> That said I think you're really overestimating the rarity of getting Gifts outside of your lodges affinity, as well as how much effort and Experience it takes. It just takes two more Experience dots to open the Gift and a sacred hunt. Once you get that down extra facets cost the same as Affinity Gifts would. My own character had two non-Affinity Gifts, with five facets between them. All of the example werewolves in the book have multiple Non-Affinity Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T07:43:03-07:00","id":1146335,"title":"","content":"Of course anyone can do anything they like, afterall I made this topic for personal reason, if it helps other people put there, even better, I don't remember trying convince anyone for anything, I don't get why you come up with the yours and mine things.<br /> <br /> Its ok not agreeing with an idea, but don't say things like, ''don't expect to be followed'', threads are to be followed by anyone who cares about the topic, if you don't care don't paricipate, no hard feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T09:30:21-07:00","id":1146362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1146335#post1146335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its ok not agreeing with an idea, but don't say things like, ''don't expect to be followed'', threads are to be followed by anyone who cares about the topic, if you don't care don't paricipate, no hard feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see. I didn't mean don't expect the thread to be followed. I meant don't expect other people would use the same 'this is a one tribe-only Gift' thing. Sorry for that, I can be unclear at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-03-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T10:03:32-07:00","id":1146367,"title":"","content":"Coolness !!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T08:23:16-07:00","id":1148591,"title":"","content":"Ok everyone, here's the moment you were all waiting for!<br /> <br /> <u><b>Gift of the Slayer Wolf </b></u><br /> <b>Shifting Urge (Cunning)</b>: The gift may be used while shapeshifting in urshul or urhan, spend 1 Essence (R) and roll manipulation+ subterfuge + Cunning - Stamina + Primal Urge, the enemy takes the form the character just shifted in and stays in that form for as along as the gift user remains also in that same form.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b><b>:</b> the prey gains the Stunned tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Rip Apart (Glory): </b>The werewolf must initiate a grapple with fangs and claws and make damage at the same time, as long as his fangs and claws rip the victim appart while grappling, its wounds may not be healed by any means, if the victim manages to break free its wounds may be healed normally, the effects of the gift are permanent.<br /> <br /> <b>Presence of the Slayer Wolf (Honor): </b>Spend one essence (Inst) and roll Presence + Intimidatikon + Honor. Any one who sees the gift user and fails a Composure + Primal Urge gains the Demoralized condition which cannot be resolved as long as the victim is in the user's presence.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The victim enters basu-im and runs away from the gift user. Victims allready in basu-im instinctively run away.<br /> <br /> <b>Brutality (Purity):</b> Spend on essence (reflexive) any time you make a bite or claw attack, your attack, deals a tilt on one of enemy's limbs. choose arm wrack, or legg wrack tilt. You simply don't need to make a Specified target attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Savage Spirit \u200b(Wisdom): </b>With a vicious snapping of the werewolf's jaws, one essence point and a roll of intelligence + occult + Wisdom ( Instant) vs composure + Primal Urge, the prey gains the Essence Overload condition for the rest of the scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b><b>: </b>The werewolf gains one essence point every turn, for one turn per wisdom renown he owns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 10-10-2017, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T08:38:34-07:00","id":1148595,"title":"","content":"Shifting Urge: Resisted rolls only substract 1 attribute. Contested rolls are different. Also, if you're making it resisted, you should limit it to a number of turns equal to successes. If it is contested, keep the mirroring form thing.<br /> <br /> Rip Apart: Several things: 1) The rules in grappling with lupine jaws already establish they can bite, and grapple at the same time. 2) You can save like 50% of word count by stating simply &quot;while grappling, your opponents cannot regenerate&quot;. I'd add the caveat to allow gauru to regen, regardless. 3) &quot;Appart&quot; isn't a word.<br /> <br /> Brutality intrudes in Urshul design space.<br /> <br /> Probably should name the gift &quot;Presence of the Wolf Slayer&quot;. Should probably mention how to prevent the gift from targeting packmates. Restrict it to single target? Up to Honor in targets? Make a condition for trying to flee while in Kuruth?<br /> <br /> Savage Spirit: Word it like Lay Low the Challenger.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in the gift description (not the facets) clarify these only work on Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T09:19:24-07:00","id":1148605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1148595#post1148595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifting Urge: Resisted rolls only substract 1 attribute. Contested rolls are different. Also, if you're making it resisted, you should limit it to a number of turns equal to successes. If it is contested, keep the mirroring form thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As it is written in the book yes it does, then just remove stamina from the roll and voila.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1148595#post1148595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rip Apart: Several things: 1) The rules in grappling with lupine jaws already establish they can bite, and grapple at the same time. 2) You can save like 50% of word count by stating simply &quot;while grappling, your opponents cannot regenerate&quot;. I'd add the caveat to allow gauru to regen, regardless. 3) &quot;Appart&quot; isn't a word.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Not all players are familiar to the 2nd edition rules. no regeration in gauru sorry, this facet is specifically for that purpose. Plus in order for the facet to work you must sink claw or fang to flesh and deal damage while establishing a grapple, which can happen only in the 3 woolf like forms and maybe to the more human ones with partial transformation, if you have the wolf facet.<br /> Edit done</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1148595#post1148595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brutality intrudes in Urshul design space.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> You need to spend essence for every time you use it so its fine. Lucky urshul that has one free use.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1148595#post1148595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably should name the gift &quot;Presence of the Wolf Slayer&quot;. Should probably mention how to prevent the gift from targeting packmates. Restrict it to single target? Up to Honor in targets? Make a condition for trying to flee while in Kuruth?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well the facet is intended to be used against prey, not packmates. in order for a packmate to become target for this facet he must become hostile to the gift user. Its an aura gift so it prob should affect all targets in 10 yard radious per Honor, that sounds better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1148595#post1148595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Savage Spirit: Word it like Lay Low the Challenger.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Nyaaahh savage must be savage even to the spirit ways.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1136195-character-tribal-and-auspice-gift-transfer-from-1st-to-2nd-edition?p=1148595#post1148595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhere in the gift description (not the facets) clarify these only work on Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is the original idea, but it can be easily used on other theriomorphs and maaaaaybe to enemies with similar traits.But so far it is only intended to kill werewolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T10:31:41-07:00","id":1148621,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a> Not addressing you. Making notes of my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}